--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party material referenced by this project
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. WebAssembly Core Specification 1.0 / 2.0 (W3C Recommendation)
   Used as the normative definition of the binary format, instruction
   semantics and value types implemented by decode/, analyze/ and emit/.
   Specification text is not copied; only its behaviour is implemented.
   https://www.w3.org/TR/wasm-core-1/

2. "Relooper: Refactoring Conditional Branching into Loops"
   Alon Zakai, Technical Report, 2011 (the structuring algorithm behind
   Emscripten's relooper). The control-flow structuring in reloop/ is an
   independent implementation of the published algorithm; no source code
   from Emscripten, Binaryen or LLVM is copied.
   https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/blob/main/docs/paper.pdf

3. wabt (WebAssembly Binary Toolkit)
   Used **at development time only**, as an external oracle: `wasm2wat`
   output is compared against moonlift's own disassembly to catch decoder
   bugs, and `wat2wasm` assembles hand-written fixtures. wabt is not linked,
   not vendored, and not required at runtime or in the test suite's pass
   criteria. Licensed Apache-2.0.
   https://github.com/WebAssembly/wabt

4. MoonBit core library (`moonbitlang/core`)
   Distributed with the MoonBit toolchain, Apache-2.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test corpus provenance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every file under corpus/ must carry an entry in corpus/PROVENANCE.md stating
its origin (generated by tools/, hand-written, or downloaded), the exact
command or URL, its license, and its SHA-256. Downloaded binaries are never
committed without that entry.
